Therefore, calm yourself, he said, this state will end to make you pass on to other steps of my humanity. Now, notice it's a journey and when you succeed in passing one exam, you will be brought to the next stage.

325
01:00:03.000 --> 01:00:18.000
Well, that's what happens in school all the time, isn't it? You put a child into school at the age of four, and nobody's ever satisfied with what they learn. When they manage one year, you shove them to a higher level and a higher level and a higher level.

326
01:00:18.000 --> 01:00:25.000
And then they graduate from primary school and you shove them into secondary and they become a junior, having been a senior.

327
01:00:25.000 --> 01:00:31.000
We don't realize that what happens to us spiritually is mirrored in our everyday life.

328
01:00:31.000 --> 01:00:40.000
And when they manage to work their way through the secondary school and they graduate from that, then they become a junior in the university.

329
01:00:40.000 --> 01:00:49.000
So each level has important stages to it, but then when you get to a higher level, you start all over again.

330
01:00:49.000 --> 01:00:58.000
And it appears as if you haven't got anywhere, in actual fact you have, because you wouldn't get to the secondary if you hadn't passed through the primary.

331
01:00:58.000 --> 01:01:03.000
You wouldn't get to the university if you hadn't passed through the secondary.

332
01:01:03.000 --> 01:01:12.000
And so he said, when you feel that you can take no more, abandon yourself more in me.

333
01:01:12.000 --> 01:01:17.000
Now notice the secret is deeper and deeper abandonment.

334
01:01:17.000 --> 01:01:28.000
And while you feel your Jesus praying, suffering and repairing, sorry, and then you will feel your Jesus repairing and suffering within you.

335
01:01:28.000 --> 01:01:32.000
And she will talk about that as we go on in these volumes.

336
01:01:32.000 --> 01:01:37.000
And he said, "But you, you are to follow me."

337
01:01:37.000 --> 01:01:44.000
Now isn't that exactly what Jesus said to Peter at the end of John's Gospel in John 21?

338
01:01:44.000 --> 01:01:52.000
When Jesus told Peter what was going to happen to himself, and then he said, "What about John?"

339
01:01:52.000 --> 01:01:58.000
And he said, "Never mind what happens to John. You follow me."

340
01:01:58.000 --> 01:02:01.000
And this is very important for all of us.

341
01:02:01.000 --> 01:02:10.000
We can waste time looking around to see what's going on in other people and how other people are getting on, and we can forget to go forward ourselves.

342
01:02:10.000 --> 01:02:14.000
He says, "No, your duty is to follow me."

343
01:02:14.000 --> 01:02:34.000
And this is very, very important in these terrible times that we're going through that the most important thing for God and for humanity is that we will follow the Lord absolutely, faithfully, unconditionally to the end, even if that end is martyrdom.

344
01:02:34.000 --> 01:02:38.000
And most especially if it's martyrdom.

345
01:02:38.000 --> 01:02:44.000
"And you," he said, "follow me, I will be the actor and you will be the spectator.

346
01:02:44.000 --> 01:02:52.000
